1
00:00:01,650 --> 00:00:04,050
This is Liao Shutao's story.

2
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:12,310
He never imagined that one day he would
encounter Jesus along life's journey.

3
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:19,620
Having grown up with a scientific
education, I had always felt certain of
one

4
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:19,960
thing:

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:27,415
If science and faith stood before truth
and asked it to choose, truth would

6
00:00:27,415 --> 00:00:29,720
surely side with science.

7
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:36,350
Yet truth's choice was so hard to
believe that I wondered whether my whole
life

8
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:38,700
until then had been a dream.

9
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:44,680
Liao Shutao was a man deeply shaped by
science.

10
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:48,640
During his passionate university years,

11
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:54,940
He was immersed in an atmosphere that
honored freedom and the pursuit of
truth.

12
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:00,440
Ideals and passion surged within him.

13
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:06,840
An open academic climate let him see
people in every field

14
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:13,447
ranging freely like untethered horses,
pursuing truth in the natural and social

15
00:01:13,447 --> 00:01:14,200
sciences.

16
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:23,978
Four years of university taught me to
prize rational thought, empiricism, and
an

17
00:01:23,978 --> 00:01:26,030
insistence on facts.

18
00:01:26,030 --> 00:01:33,687
I believed that only careful,
independent thought could test every
idea and

19
00:01:33,687 --> 00:01:36,750
piece of knowledge I accepted.

20
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:41,910
Only then could I develop a more mature
confidence in who I was,

21
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:47,270
and understand more deeply the meaning
and value of our existence.

22
00:01:47,950 --> 00:01:50,490
I also learned how precious freedom is.

23
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:58,101
Freedom lets human thought roam, giving
rise to the flourishing achievements of

24
00:01:58,101 --> 00:01:59,450
science today.

25
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:06,990
Because we cherish our own freedom, we
learn to set boundaries and respect the

26
00:02:06,990 --> 00:02:08,610
freedom of others.

27
00:02:08,610 --> 00:02:16,370
After graduation, military service, and
work, he married.

28
00:02:17,430 --> 00:02:23,635
The couple then moved to the United
States to study at the University of
Texas

29
00:02:23,635 --> 00:02:24,430
at Austin.

30
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:29,182
Liao pursued a master's degree in
mechanics and a doctorate in civil

31
00:02:29,182 --> 00:02:30,020
engineering.

32
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:35,320
His wife entered a doctoral program in
molecular biology and genetics.

33
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:41,710
It was a completely different country.
Everything felt fresh and full of joy.

34
00:02:43,150 --> 00:02:47,370
The beautiful, comfortable library
became his favorite place.

35
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:58,073
As he carefully pursued facts and truth,
he grew happier and more assured in his

36
00:02:58,073 --> 00:02:58,720
steps.

37
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:07,972
Something remarkable happened one day in
1994, my fifth year of study in

38
00:03:07,972 --> 00:03:09,000
America.

39
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:14,944
I came out of the university's Main
Building and suddenly felt like turning

40
00:03:14,944 --> 00:03:15,420
around

41
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:23,242
to admire its magnificent twenty-seven-
story tower. The university is famous
and

42
00:03:23,242 --> 00:03:25,100
over a century old.

43
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:30,620
As I turned to look, I suddenly noticed

44
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:37,800
a line carved into the weathered marble
above the entrance:

45
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:42,000
Ye shall know the truth and the truth
shall make you free.

46
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:48,805
At that moment, words flashed through my
mind more forcefully than the

47
00:03:48,805 --> 00:03:50,500
inscription itself:

48
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:52,460
You must seek the truth.

49
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:55,000
The truth will set you free.

50
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:02,840
Those words shook me profoundly.
Suddenly, I felt that everything made
sense.

51
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:10,724
I thought only a great philosopher of
the Renaissance could have spoken such

52
00:04:10,724 --> 00:04:12,280
timeless words.

53
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:17,200
I thought they had inspired the West to
pursue truth,

54
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:23,380
and to establish universities devoted to
that pursuit.

55
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:31,753
To me, this explained why their
scientific achievements had given them
global

56
00:04:31,753 --> 00:04:32,360
power.

57
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:37,200
I even thought I had understood the
reason for China's long-standing
weakness.

58
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:44,200
From then on, he regarded those words as
the greatest saying of all.

59
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:49,280
He admired its author as a giant among
great thinkers,

60
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:55,283
one who saw and precisely expressed the
close link between truth and freedom,

61
00:04:55,283 --> 00:04:57,700
two seemingly unrelated things.

62
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:04,520
At the end of that year, Liao completed
his doctorate.

63
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:12,260
But without warning, his family life
entered turbulent waters.

64
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:21,090
My joy at finishing my studies coincided
with the hardest period in my beloved

65
00:05:21,090 --> 00:05:23,020
wife's academic life.

66
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:29,953
She had spent six years pursuing her
doctorate, with no sign of being able to

67
00:05:29,953 --> 00:05:30,700
graduate.

68
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:37,180
She worked on experiments day and night,
only to face repeated failures.

69
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:41,040
The pressure often made her wake in the
night and cry.

70
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:47,272
Sometimes, when she woke in the morning,
there would be a clump of hair on the

71
00:05:47,272 --> 00:05:47,560
bed.

72
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:51,640
Then she became pregnant.

73
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:56,560
We were overjoyed, yet unsure how to
face the future.

74
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:03,700
In fact, whether she eventually earned
her doctorate did not matter much to me.

75
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:07,880
So I decided to return to Taiwan and
take a teaching position.

76
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:14,140
That September, I returned to Taiwan
alone to teach,

77
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:19,000
leaving her in America on her own, with
a baby on the way.

78
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,900
Our son was born in America in November.

79
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:26,760
I took two weeks' leave from Chung Hua
University to visit her.

80
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:31,680
On the evening before my leave ended,

81
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:40,980
my wife held our newborn son and said
something that hurt me deeply.

82
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:45,980
Only years later did I understand that
it had been her cry for help.

83
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:52,560
At the time, Liao returned to Taiwan
with a wounded heart.

84
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:56,040
Over the next two years, separated by
time and distance,

85
00:06:56,040 --> 00:07:00,740
he could not understand why his wife
seemed to put her career before their
love.

86
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:06,716
If graduation was so far away, why not
give up her studies and come home to be

87
00:07:06,716 --> 00:07:07,260
together?

88
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:15,580
Even phone calls across thousands of
miles could not thaw his frozen heart.

89
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:23,840
Without her emotional support, his wife
could only cry during their phone calls.

90
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:31,080
In the lab, her fellow students came to
see her as a strange Asian girl.

91
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:36,120
No one could talk with her, because she
would cry as soon as she began to speak.

92
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:39,680
She was on the verge of breaking down.

93
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:51,340
Then one day, a student from mainland
China who worked in the next lab passed

94
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,560
her door.

95
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:58,740
She felt God strongly urging her to go
inside and share the gospel.

96
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:03,900
She had been a Christian only a few
years and was afraid to go in.

97
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:12,643
But the urging persisted, so she timidly
entered the lab and shared the gospel

98
00:08:12,643 --> 00:08:14,100
with my wife.

99
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:21,080
As she read the gospel leaflet aloud and
reached the words, There is a Savior,

100
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:27,759
my wife was like a drowning person who
suddenly found a strong arm that could

101
00:08:27,759 --> 00:08:28,540
save her.

102
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:33,920
That was how she was brought into the
church, saved, and became a Christian.

103
00:08:33,920 --> 00:08:43,022
After she believed, her heart grew
stronger and more joyful. Her life
changed

104
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:44,440
wonderfully.

105
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:50,387
The brothers and sisters in the church
were not relatives, yet willingly cooked

106
00:08:50,387 --> 00:08:52,480
and brought her meals every day.

107
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:57,130
To him, this was almost beyond belief.

108
00:08:58,470 --> 00:09:02,450
The following summer, he went to America
again to visit his wife.

109
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:07,990
She often took him to church meetings
that he did not enjoy.

110
00:09:09,310 --> 00:09:14,022
Watching them earnestly read the Bible
and sing praises to God, he could not

111
00:09:14,022 --> 00:09:14,890
understand it.

112
00:09:15,950 --> 00:09:20,438
They often asked whether he enjoyed the
meetings and whether he wanted to be

113
00:09:20,438 --> 00:09:20,970
baptized.

114
00:09:22,010 --> 00:09:28,791
He was unconvinced, but they had been so
kind to his family that he did not want

115
00:09:28,791 --> 00:09:30,910
to reject their goodwill.

116
00:09:30,910 --> 00:09:33,850
So he politely put them off.

117
00:09:34,690 --> 00:09:39,350
Then came Thursday, July 23, 1998.

118
00:09:39,350 --> 00:09:41,890
I decided I would no longer let them
bother me.
